-- title:
--   Transport of a patching datum along an isomorphism R ≅ T
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring: a commutative domain that is a discrete valuation ring and is adically complete with respect to its maximal ideal. Let $\ell$ be a natural number, let $R$ be a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, and let $T$ be a nontrivial commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra that is finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module. Assume given an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi : R \to T$ whose underlying function is bijective, and assume $T$ admits a complete-intersection presentation with equally many variables and relations: there are $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$ together with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra isomorphism $\mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]/(f_1,\dots,f_n) \cong T$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a type $M$ carrying an additive group structure, a module structure over $R$, a module structure over $T$, and a nontrivial element, such that the two actions are compatible, $\varphi(x)\cdot m = x \cdot m$ for all $x \in R$, $m \in M$, and such that for some $r \in \mathbb{N}$ there is a term of [`Algebra.PatchingDatum 𝒪 ℓ r R M`](def/Algebra_PatchingDatum.html#L39), i.e. for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ a patching level for the ideal $J_n \subseteq \mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_r]]$ generated by the $(1+X_j)^{\ell^n}-1$: a module $N$ over $\mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_r]]$, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra endomorphism $\phi$ of that power series ring, a surjective $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\psi$ onto $R$ with $\psi(\phi(X_i))=0$ for all $i$, a surjective additive map $\pi : N \to M$ satisfying $\pi(f\cdot x) = \psi(f)\cdot \pi(x)$ and with kernel exactly $(\phi(X_1),\dots,\phi(X_r))\cdot N$, and a finite family $b_1,\dots,b_d \in N$ spanning $N$ over the image of $\phi$ with $\sum_i \phi(c_i)\, b_i = 0$ if and only if every $c_i$ lies in $J_n$.
--
--   This is the step that converts the output of the Taylor–Wiles construction — an isomorphism of the deformation or Hecke algebra $R$ onto a finite free complete-intersection $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $T$ — into the existential form of the patching hypothesis used later: a nontrivial module acted on compatibly by both rings, together with a patching datum for the pair $(R,M)$. It is invoked by the statements producing patching data for Hecke algebras of cusp forms and for the Galois representation data attached to Weierstrass curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_PatchingDatum_exists_module_of_bijective_of_exists_presentation.lean

